From 769f2a67747c10e7d428912aef851de796749990 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:26:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] netstack: IPv6 endpoints in socket paths, DNS server from
 router advertisements

Socket paths take and show IPv6 endpoints in brackets ([fe80::1]:5353),
so programs can open IPv6 UDP and TCP sockets. The RDNSS option of a
router advertisement (RFC 8106) gives an IPv6 name server, shown in
/scheme/netcfg/resolv/nameserver6.
---
